                          GE card — image plane control:                                               
                            GE 0 : no image plane (free space)                                         
                            GE 1 : activate image plane at z=0 (required for any ground run)           
                                                                                                       
                          GN card — ground parameters (IPERF field):                                   
                            GN -1 : nullify prior ground, set free space (all other fields ignored)    
                            GN  1 : perfectly conducting PEC (epsilon/sigma fields ignored)            
                            GN  2 : real ground, Sommerfeld/Norton                                     
                                     F1 = relative permittivity epsilon_r                              
                                          dry soil=3  average=13  wet=20  sea water=80                 
                                     F2 = conductivity sigma [S/m]                                     
                                          dry=0.001   average=0.005  wet=0.02  sea=4.0                 
                                                                                                       
                          Correct GE+GN combinations:                                                  
                            Free space  : GE 0        (no GN card)                                     
                            Perfect PEC : GE 1 + GN 1                                                  
                            Real ground : GE 1 + GN 2 epsilon_r sigma                                  
                            Note: GE 0 + GN 2 is a common error — misses near-field ground coupling    
                                                                                                       
                          EX card — structure excitation:                                              
                            EX  I1  I2  I3  I4  F1        F2                                           
                                |   |   |   |   |         |                                            
                                |   |   |   |   |         +-- F2: imaginary part of voltage [V]        
                                |   |   |   |   |              (= V * sin(phase_deg))                  
                                |   |   |   |   +------------ F1: real part of voltage [V]             
                                |   |   |   |                  (= V * cos(phase_deg))                  
                                |   |   |   +---------------- I4: print flag (0=suppress, 1=print      
                                |   |   |                         currents near source segment)        
                                |   |   +-------------------- I3: segment number within the wire       
                                |   |                              (1 = first/start segment)           
                                |   |                              (N = last/end segment)              
                                |   +------------------------ I2: wire tag number (from GW card)       
                                +---------------------------- I1: excitation type                      
                                     0 = voltage source (applied-E-field)  <-- NeoMoM default          
                                     1 = incident plane wave, linear polarization                      
                                     2 = incident plane wave, right-hand elliptic polarization         
                                     3 = incident plane wave, left-hand elliptic polarization          
                                     4 = elementary current source                                     
                                     5 = voltage source (current-slope-discontinuity)                  
                                                                                                       
                            NeoMoM always uses I1=0 (voltage source) with 1V at the feed node.         
                            F1=V*cos(phase), F2=V*sin(phase) for complex voltage excitation.           
                            For 1V at 0 degrees: F1=1.0, F2=0.0                                        
                                                                                                       
                          RP card — radiation pattern request:                                         
                            RP  IOPT  NTHETA  NPHI  XNDA  THETA0  PHI0  DTHETA  DPHI                   
                                |     |       |     |     |       |     |       |                      
                                |     |       |     |     |       |     |       +-- PHI increment (deg)
                                |     |       |     |     |       |     +---------- THETA increment (de
                                |     |       |     |     |       +---------------- PHI start (deg)    
                                |     |       |     |     +------------------------ THETA start (deg)  
                                |     |       |     |       0=zenith  90=horizon                       
                                |     |       |     +------------------------------ XNDA output format 
                                |     |       |       1000=power gain dBi no norm  0000=normalised     
                                |     |       +------------------------------------ NPHI: phi steps    
                                |     +------------------------------------------- NTHETA: theta steps 
                                +------------------------------------------------- IOPT: 0=far-field   
                                                                                                       
                            This card: azimuth cut at theta=90 (horizon), phi=0 to 360, step=5 deg     
